WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.660
Making a movie isn't child's play — even
for a child actor.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.940
Throughout Hollywood history, kids in the
industry have been called upon to act in harrowing

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.230
roles that push the limits of their abilities,
and according to some critics, the boundaries

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.100
of good taste.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:18.200
Here are some of the most famous examples
of underage actors in mature roles.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.660
Dakota Fanning, Hounddog

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.040
In 2007, 12 year-old Fanning shocked critics
and viewing audiences alike by taking the

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:30.300
role of the neglected, abused Lewellen in
this coming-of-age drama — which includes

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.960
a scene in which her character is taken.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:36.550
Though the violent act is strictly implied
with shots of Fanning's face and hands, the

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.420
film was subject to intense backlash from
viewers, critics, and activist groups who

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.620
felt that the young actress shouldn't have
been allowed to join the production.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.480
Fanning responded to the criticism by pushing
back, saying, "It's a movie and it's called

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.300
acting.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.880
[...] I wanted to do the film because I thought
it might help one person that has happened

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.460
to and help them overcome adversity in their
lives."

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:58.760
Unfortunately, Fanning's hopes of reaching
abuse survivors were effectively undermined

00:00:58.769 --> 00:01:01.489
by the controversy, which killed the film's
buzz.

00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:06.980
Hounddog only earned $131,000 against its
$3 million budget after a limited release.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.440
Natalie Portman, The Professional

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.960
Seventeen years before she danced her way
to an Oscar win, Portman made her big-screen

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:18.371
debut in this 1993 thriller as Mathilda, a
little girl whose family is taken by a

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.720
corrupt DEA agent.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.340
When she takes refuge with a neighbor — who
happens to be a hitman — he becomes her

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:28.260
mentor in all things vengeance, a relationship
tinged by an uneasy chemistry between the

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:28.760
two.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.600
At twelve years old, Portman was the exact
same age as the character she was playing

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:36.960
— and watching her smoke, shoot, and even
hold a gun to her own head made for a shocking

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.700
spectacle, albeit one that proved she was
a star who could handle the most challenging

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.420
roles out there.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.100
"One shot, not bad.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:43.600
Huh?"

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.420
Kirsten Dunst, Interview with the Vampire

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:52.000
This list wouldn't be complete without this
chilling performance by Dunst, in one of her

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.980
very first feature film roles.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.820
In Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles, Dunst's
character Claudia was only five years old

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.640
when she was turned into a vampire — but
even for Hollywood, that would have been pushing

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.140
it.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.140
Instead, the role went to the eleven year-old
actress, who went all-out to capture the anger,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:12.129
violence, and near-insanity of an adult woman
who's trapped for eternity in the body of

00:02:12.129 --> 00:02:12.880
a little girl.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.400
As disturbing as it was to see Dunst tackle
the challenging material, she did do an amazing

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.400
job, earning a Golden Globe nomination and
a permanent spot on the A-list for her performance.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.040
Christian Bale, Empire of the Sun

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.250
Long before he became famous for American
Psycho, The Machinist, or The Dark Knight

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:35.069
trilogy, Christian Bale won critical acclaim
for playing the role of Jim in the 1987 Steven

00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:37.240
Spielberg war film Empire of the Sun.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:41.840
The movie is essentially a coming-of-age drama
set during Japan's occupation of China during

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:46.120
World War II, and Bale was just thirteen when
he took on the challenging role of a boy who

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.030
goes from living a comfortable life with his
family in Shanghai to growing up behind the

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:52.400
barbed wire of a Japanese internment camp.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.920
Spielberg doesn't pull any punches with Empire
of the Sun, and despite being just a child

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:01.720
himself, Bale delivers an emotional and commanding
performance as a boy faced with the horrors

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.220
of war.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.860
Macaulay Culkin, The Good Son

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:09.880
Evil kids have been a staple of thriller and
horror movies over the years, but that didn't

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:14.340
stop audiences from being alarmed by the sight
of little Kevin McCallister from Home Alone

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.860
playing this cold-blooded, pint-sized psychopath
in The Good Son.

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:21.300
There's no supernatural element driving Henry's
penchant for mayhem.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.680
He's just plain bad.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.920
When his cousin Mark, played by Elijah Wood,
comes to visit Henry's family during winter

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.360
vacation, things turn decidedly dark.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:33.480
It's hard to decide what's more disturbing
— watching a 12-year-old try to take everyone

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.260
that crosses him…

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:36.680
"Don't f--- with me"

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.240
...or trying to pretend that it wasn't hilarious
to watch this same little kid perpetrate savage

00:03:44.249 --> 00:03:48.819
acts of violence against two bumbling criminals
in a John Hughes Christmas comedy just three

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:49.580
years earlier.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.080
"Ah"

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.400
Because of the obvious Home Alone parallels,
The Good Son wasn't really scary enough to

00:03:59.409 --> 00:04:04.459
make anyone scream… except maybe Culkin's
parents, who had to watch Macaulay very convincingly

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:08.080
attempt to murder his real-life little sister
Quinn in scenes like this one.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.620
Jodie Foster, Taxi Driver

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:15.780
Foster stirred up quite a controversy when
she appeared as child walker Iris in Martin

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.180
Scorsese's 1976 classic Taxi Driver.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.120
"You talkin to me?"

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.740
While not the central figure of the film,
Iris still plays an important part when her

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:29.539
path crosses with the troubled Travis Bickle,
played by Robert De Niro — and Foster was

00:04:29.539 --> 00:04:31.520
just twelve when she played the role.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.520
For that reason, Scorsese took precautions:
his young star was subjected to psych evaluations

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:40.920
to make sure she could handle the job, and
her older sister Connie was used as a stand-in

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.740
for suggestive scenes.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.580
Olivia Hussey and Claire Danes, Romeo &amp; Juliet

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.380
Shakespeare's famous play centers on a pair
of star-crossed teenage lovers — but it's

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.940
also full of sex, violence, and ending.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:58.260
That means that casting actual teenagers in
the lead roles has historically raised some

00:04:58.260 --> 00:04:58.760
eyebrows.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:05.060
First came Franco Zeffirelli's 1968 adaptation,
in which actress Olivia Hussey was only 15,

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.380
and her Romeo, Leonard Whiting, was 17.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:12.340
Thirty years later, director Baz Luhrmann
went with an older Romeo in the form of Leonardo

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.680
DiCaprio, who was 21 at the time.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:19.240
But Claire Danes, who played Juliet, was just
16 — which made her two years older than

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:23.810
her character, but in some folks' opinions,
still much too young to be playing a scene

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.260
like this onscreen.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:27.780
Jacob Reynolds, Gummo

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:34.060
Not many entries on this list can top 1997's
experimental dystopian art film Gummo when

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.000
it comes to making audiences squirm.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:40.440
Written and directed by Harmony Korine, Gummo
chronicles the lives of several residents

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.960
of Xenia, Ohio, following the effects of a
devastating tornado.

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:48.800
The movie comprises an interconnected series
of scenes that offer a glimpse into depravity,

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:53.020
demoralization, and the depths of poverty
— with a linchpin performance by thirteen

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:57.460
year-old Jacob Reynolds as Solomon, a kid
whose hobbies include taking cats, huffing

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.720
glue, and paying a developmentally disabled
girl to have relations with him.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.600
Most critics panned Gummo for its pervasive
graphic content, but it was lauded by a few

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:09.720
filmmakers, including famed director Werner
Herzog —who particularly liked this scene

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.260
featuring Solomon chowing down on junk food
in a bathtub.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.400
Sue Lyon and Dominique Swain, Lolita

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.280
The premise of Vladimir Nabokov's classic
novel about a middle-aged man's  obsession

00:06:21.289 --> 00:06:25.380
with an adolescent girl makes it tough to
adapt for the screen — especially when it

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:27.180
comes to casting the title character.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.400
But that hasn't stopped directors from trying.

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:34.120
In 1962, Stanley Kubrick did a more oblique
take on the material, with James Mason as

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.610
Humbert Humbert and Sue Lyon as Lolita.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:40.819
At fourteen, Lyon was two years older than
her character, and Kubrick was careful to

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:43.200
skirt the  content of Nabokov's novel.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:45.480
"Have you told her anything about us?"

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.080
"No, have you?"

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.060
But the film and Lyon's role in it still proved
controversial.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:55.280
And this is one topic that hasn't become less
of a hot potato with the passage of time:

00:06:55.560 --> 00:07:00.280
when director Adrian Lyne made his own Lolita
more than thirty years later, with 15-year-old

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:04.039
Dominique Swain in the title role, the movie
was forced to premiere on cable when it couldn't

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:08.220
find an American distributor — and critics
in England even tried to get the film banned.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.680
The entire cast of Kids

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:15.500
This film centers on the lives of several
teenagers — and their lives — during

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:20.470
the height of the AIDS epidemic, and it doesn't
shy away from showing teenagers in some seriously

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:21.940
disturbing situations.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:26.440
The characters in Kids engage in a lot of
risky behaviors, from doing drugs to having

00:07:26.449 --> 00:07:31.570
unprotected with folks, and
the cast was made up entirely of teenagers,

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:35.820
which made for plenty of controversy when
the film premiered with an NC-17 rating.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:38.960
All these years later, it's still a polarizing
work of art.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:42.020
Brooke Shields, Pretty Baby and The Blue Lagoon

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:47.080
As a girl, actress Brooke Shields appeared
in two different movies that placed her front-and-center

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.960
in the debate about children and on-screen
stuff.

00:07:50.289 --> 00:07:54.300
At age 12, she starred in Pretty Baby as a
child prostitute living with her mother in

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.160
a New Orleans brothel at the turn of the 20th
century.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:01.710
The film — and Shields'  in it — was
criticized by many, and the movie was even

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.780
banned in two Canadian provinces.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:09.960
"Well you certainly did it, didn't you?"

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:14.539
However, the backlash didn't put the actress
off controversial material; just two years

00:08:14.539 --> 00:08:18.419
later, Shields appeared in The Blue Lagoon
as a shipwrecked girl growing up on an island

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:21.580
with only her cousin, played Christopher Atkins,
for company.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:25.819
As they reach puberty, they eventually fall
in love, and even have a child — a plot

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:30.400
point which raised eyebrows, as did several
scenes involving the fourteen year-old

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:30.900
Shields.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:33.460
Linda Blair, The Exorcist

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:38.740
Widely recognized as one of the greatest horror
movies of the 20th century, The Exorcist was

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:43.430
also extremely controversial, with famed critic
Roger Ebert even suggesting it deserved an

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:48.100
"X" rating instead of the "R" it was given
by the MPAA — even though he loved it.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:52.400
That's partly because of its horrifying subject
matter, but the presence of an actual thirteen

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:57.100
year-old girl in the role of the possessed
Regan MacNeil was also considered problematic.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:01.720
Linda Blair's performance was central to some
of the most disturbing, disgusting, obscene,

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:06.300
and vulgar sequences in the film, although
she pushed back against rumors that being

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.480
in the movie had psychologically scarred her.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.980
She explained: "A lot of untruthful stories
were made up about me being mentally disturbed

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:13.990
by the movie.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:16.660
I never was because I never bought into the
whole Devil thing."

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:21.700
Instead, it was the physical demands of The
Exorcist that had a prolonged impact; Blair

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:25.800
fractured her spine while filming this levitation
scene, an injury that would later develop

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:30.440
into scoliosis and cause the actress ongoing
health problems well into adulthood.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.780
Tatum O'Neal, Paper Moon

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:38.420
This 1973 comedy-drama is a lot more tame
than some of the other entries on this list,

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:43.120
but it definitely has its moments — like
this one, where its nine year-old star casually

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.020
enjoys a cigarette before bedtime.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:49.360
Tatum O'Neal and real-life father, Ryan O'Neal,
play characters named Addie and Mose, a pair

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.740
of unlikely partners in crime on a cross-country
road trip.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:57.310
Throughout the film, we watch the absolutely
tiny Tatum smoke, drink, and con people out

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:59.020
of their money like an old pro.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:03.360
And when Mose starts to neglect Addie in favor
of an "exotic dancer" named Trixie, played

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:08.040
by Madeline Kahn, the jealous girl even devises
her own con to get Trixie dumped.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:12.240
The movie might have been more controversial
if Tatum hadn't been so talented in the role;

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:16.570
her performance earned widespread acclaim,
and she ultimately won an Academy Award for

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:20.100
the part, making her the youngest competitive
Oscar winner in history.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:22.620
Chloe Moretz: Kick-Ass

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:28.160
At the age of 11, Moretz landed her most controversial
role: vigilante superhero Hit-Girl in the

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:29.680
2010 movie Kick-Ass.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:33.800
Compared to most little girls — and also
to most grown men and women — Hit-Girl is

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:38.139
a hardened and nihilistic figure, punctuating
her frequent murders with obscenity-laden

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:38.820
one-liners.

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:43.260
Kick-Ass met with backlash for its violence
and language, with many critics especially

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:48.160
horrified by Moretz's character, and it received
a well-deserved "R" rating from the MPAA...

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:53.140
which meant that its most hardcore tween-aged
hero wasn't able to watch herself drop f-bombs

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:55.340
in Kick-Ass without adult supervision.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.920
"Ohhhhkay, geez!"

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:02.960
Thanks for watching!

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.070
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
